# Workflow rules (implemented in backend/src/domain — change them there, nowhere else)

## Roles (role_code)
CLINIC_STAFF (scoped to their clinic via user_clinic_scope) · COORD_INTERNAL · COORD_INTERNATIONAL · IT_ADMIN.
MOH, MOD and external providers have **no accounts**.

## Visibility (access.js)
- Draft → creator only.
- Clinic Staff → requests where their clinic is the requesting clinic, or (Internal only) the receiving clinic.
- Coordination – Internal → all Internal requests. Coordination – International → all External KSA + International.
- IT Admin → no request data; Admin Settings only.

## Status flow (workflow.js `RULES`)
| Action | From | Who | To |
|---|---|---|---|
| submit | Draft | creator (Clinic Staff) | Internal → PendingClinicResponse; otherwise → PendingProviderEmail |
| approve / reject | PendingClinicResponse | Clinic Staff at the receiving clinic (Internal) | Confirmed / Rejected |
| sendToProvider | PendingProviderEmail | Coordination – International | SentToProviderAwaitingResponse |
| resendToProvider | SentToProviderAwaitingResponse | Coordination – International | (no change) |
| recordProviderApproved / Declined | SentToProviderAwaitingResponse | Coordination – International | Confirmed / Rejected |
| withdraw | any active status | Clinic Staff at the requesting clinic | Withdrawn |
| complete | Confirmed, after travel end date | the coordination team that owns the destination type | Completed |
| comment | any non-draft | anyone who can view | — |
Rejected, Withdrawn, Completed are terminal (DB trigger also blocks changes). Nothing ever returns to Draft.

## Validation (validation.js)
- National ID / Iqama: exactly 10 digits. Passport: 6–9 letters/digits. MRN: digits only.
- Travel start not in the past (Asia/Riyadh "today"); end strictly after start; sessions = whole number ≥ 1.
- Files: PDF/JPG/PNG ≤ 10 MB; MOH/MOD approvals and provider replies also accept EML.
- Required at submit: MOH approval, medical report, ID copy; MOD approval only when "MOD approval applies" is ticked.
- Reject/decline reason: 10–500 characters. Confirmed session dates: within requested travel dates ± 2 days.

## SLA / reminders
`sla_rule` stages: PendingClinicResponse, PendingProviderEmail, SentToProviderAwaitingResponse, Completion (days after
travel end). Overdue = days on current step > target. `jobs/reminders.js` notifies at most once per reminder frequency.

## Notifications
Use `notify()` inside the transaction (in-portal row + optional templated email row), and let `runAction` flush emails
after commit. Template codes live in `notification_template`; merge fields are listed in `MERGE_FIELDS`.
